rows.en:
There stood the Mummy Man.
"Waaaaah!"
His scream echoed through the whole school.{p}

I see.
Then, so that you'll come to like movies, {a}, shall I lend you a good video sometime?
I think movies are a wonderful thing.{p}

All that was left was the editing.
You take the scenes shot separately and splice them together one by one.
Apparently it's really hard work.{p}

This time there was no doubt about it: he had never shot a scene like this.
But it was truly well done.
So, without hesitation, he edited that scene in too, and put it in the final cut.{p}

When he thought that, he wanted to keep editing more than anything else.
And the film he watched that day showed something even stranger.
It was the scene where the hero takes down one assassin after another on his way to defeat the organization's boss.{p}

I started to feel very sick.
I happened to look up.
On the white wall I'd been using as a screen, Tokita's mangled body was still showing...{p}

Just then, Tokita lifted his crushed face and looked at me.
It was so sudden that my legs froze and I couldn't move.
And then Tokita leapt out of the white wall.{p}

Then one day, during work on the school's sewage tank, a strange stone came up out of the ground.
Apparently there were records of a meteorite falling here long ago, so people figured this stone was that meteorite.
So it was decided that it would be investigated at a later date, and the construction was halted.{p}

The old school building didn't have a very good reputation, so Tokita hesitated a little.
But because of that meteorite, his hopes outweighed his unease.
He went into the old school building and peeked into the classroom nearest the entrance.{p}

The creature was there, and it was eating something.
It was crunching away on something like a red stick.
After chewing for a while, the creature spat something out.{p}
